    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0646" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3778</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Denby</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic">March 28,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith for
                    your information a copy of despatch No. 479 of January 28, 1921,<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d473-f1"/> from the American Consulate General at Shanghai regarding
                    conditions of foreign residence in the Interior of China, particularly in the
                    Yangtsze Valley.</p>
                <pb facs="0647" n="523" xml:id="pg523"/>
                <p>The Department would be glad to receive an expression of opinion from you as to
                    the feasibility of arrangements for increasing the Naval forces in that section
                    of China, as is suggested in the enclosed despatch.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles E. Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
